Guiding Principles
One shop, one admin. No multi-vendor logic anywhere — keep models simple.
Cart lives in the browser. localStorage only, until Orders exist.
Admin controls everything content-related (products, categories, brands, QR image) — zero hardcoded data in the frontend.
Backend is the source of truth. Frontend never trusts its own state for anything security-relevant (prices, stock, auth).
Build backend-first per resource (model → controller → routes → test with Postman/Thunder Client), then wire the frontend to it. This means you always know whether a bug is backend or frontend.
Every phase ends with something visibly working. No phase should end with "half-built and untestable."
