Why this shape: every resource (Product, Category, Brand, Settings) gets a matching model → controller → route on the backend and api file → components → pages on the frontend. When you add Order/Payment later, you add the same five files on each side — nothing existing gets restructured.

B. Database Schema

User

{ name, email, password (hashed), role: 'admin', createdAt }

Only one admin user is expected, but keep role on the schema now — costs nothing and means you don't need a migration if you ever add staff logins.

Category

{ name, slug, createdAt }

Brand

{ name, slug, logo (optional), createdAt }

Product

{
  name, slug, description, price,
  category: ObjectId → Category,
  brand: ObjectId → Brand,
  images: [ { url, publicId } ],
  sizes: [String],           // e.g. ["S","M","L","XL"]
  colors: [String],
  stock: Number,
  featured: Boolean,
  isNew: Boolean,
  createdAt, updatedAt
}

Settings (a single document — no admin needs more than one shop record)

{
  shopName, aboutText,
  phone, whatsappNumber, address, mapEmbedUrl,
  openingHours, instagramUrl, facebookUrl,
  paymentQr: { url, publicId }
}

Relationships: Product → Category (many-to-one), Product → Brand (many-to-one). Category and Brand are referenced by ObjectId and populated on read — this is what lets "add a category from the admin panel" work without touching Product code.

Future (not built now): Order { user?, items: [{product, qty, size, color, priceAtPurchase}], total, status, paymentProof }, Payment { order, method, status, transactionRef }. Because cart items already carry {productId, qty, size, color} (see section H), turning a cart into an Order later is a straight mapping, not a redesign.

C. REST API List

Base URL: /api

Method	Endpoint	Purpose	Auth	Request Body	Response (example)
POST	/auth/login	Admin login	No	{ email, password }	{ token, admin: {name, email} }
GET	/auth/me	Get logged-in admin	Yes	—	{ name, email, role }
GET	/products	List products (search/filter/sort/paginate via query params)	No	—	{ products: [...], total, page }
GET	/products/:idOrSlug	Single product	No	—	{ product }
POST	/products	Create product	Admin	{ name, description, price, category, brand, sizes, colors, stock, featured, isNew } + images	{ product }
PUT	/products/:id	Update product	Admin	any subset of fields	{ product }
DELETE	/products/:id	Delete product	Admin	—	{ message }
GET	/categories	List categories	No	—	{ categories: [...] }
POST	/categories	Create category	Admin	{ name }	{ category }
PUT	/categories/:id	Update category	Admin	{ name }	{ category }
DELETE	/categories/:id	Delete category	Admin	—	{ message }
GET	/categories/:id/products	Products in a category	No	—	{ products: [...] }
GET	/brands	List brands	No	—	{ brands: [...] }
POST	/brands	Create brand	Admin	{ name, logo? }	{ brand }
PUT	/brands/:id	Update brand	Admin	{ name, logo? }	{ brand }
DELETE	/brands/:id	Delete brand	Admin	—	{ message }
GET	/settings	Get shop info/QR/contact	No	—	{ settings }
PUT	/settings	Update shop info	Admin	any subset of Settings fields	{ settings }
PUT	/settings/qr	Replace payment QR image	Admin	multipart image	{ settings }

